# app/cluster-env.local.example -- template for SITE-LOCAL cluster settings.
#
#   cp app/cluster-env.local.example app/cluster-env.local.sh    # gitignored
#
# app/cluster-env.sh sources app/cluster-env.local.sh AFTER its silverback
# defaults are assigned and BEFORE anything is applied, so set only what
# differs here. Use plain bash assignments. Never `exit`. The file must
# return 0: a syntax error or a failing last command fails every job with
# "Error: cluster-env: ... cluster-env.local.sh failed" (end the file with
# `true` if its last line is a conditional). Silverback needs no local file.
#
# The file is per checkout (gitignored): copy it into every deployment (prod,
# staging) and every worktree; a checkout without it silently uses the
# silverback defaults. To share one file, symlink app/cluster-env.local.sh to
# it in each checkout.
#
# Set DM_ENV_* here, not in pm2.config.js or the service environment: inherited
# DM_ENV_* values are ignored (and reported with a WARNING).
#
# Check syntax:  bash -n app/cluster-env.local.sh
# Verify a run:  the job .out shows "cluster-env: applying site overrides from ..."
#                and "cluster-env: found libmpi.so.40 at ...". Any unknown
#                DM_ENV_* name is reported as a WARNING (typo guard).
#                Any "WARNING: cluster-env: ... not found" line means the
#                override is wrong, EVEN IF the job succeeded: the server's
#                inherited LD_LIBRARY_PATH (forwarded by sbatch --export=ALL)
#                may be masking it. To test the override on its own, submit
#                once with `env -u LD_LIBRARY_PATH sbatch ...`.
# Every analysis wrapper picks this up. Never edit app/<analysis>/*.sh for
# environment reasons.

# Where HyPhy's OpenMPI + UCX shared libraries live (':'-separated). This is
# the setting that matters. When it is wrong, HYPHYMPI fails with
# "libmpi.so.40: cannot open shared object file" (exit 127) -- but only if the
# server's inherited LD_LIBRARY_PATH does not happen to hold MPI libs; the
# WARNING line in the job .out is the authoritative signal. To find the
# directories:  ldd .hyphy/HYPHYMPI | grep 'not found'
# Leave it empty ("") only if MPI is already on the system loader path. (The
# srun task then sees LD_LIBRARY_PATH=":..."; the empty entry is harmless.)
#DM_ENV_MPI_LIB_DIRS="/opt/openmpi-5.0.7/lib:/opt/ucx-1.18/lib"

# Environment modules, loaded in order; loading stops at the first failure.
# "" = load none.
#DM_ENV_MODULES="gcc/14 openmpi/5.0.7"

# lmod / Environment Modules init script. Loads are skipped on nodes where
# this file does not exist.
#DM_ENV_LMOD_INIT="/usr/share/lmod/lmod/init/bash"

# Appended after the inherited LD_LIBRARY_PATH (silverback: /usr/lib64).
# "" = append nothing.
#DM_ENV_LD_APPEND=""

# Prepended to PATH (silverback: /usr/local/bin, where the system hyphy lives).
#DM_ENV_PATH_PREPEND="/opt/hyphy/bin"

# Libraries expected in DM_ENV_MPI_LIB_DIRS. Diagnostic only: a missing
# library produces a warning in the job log.
#DM_ENV_REQUIRED_LIBS="libmpi.so.40 libucp.so.0"

# Extra runtime environment: this file is sourced into the batch shell, so
# exports here reach every srun task (MPI transport / MCA settings), e.g.
#export UCX_TLS=rc,sm,self
#export OMPI_MCA_pml=ucx
#export OMPI_MCA_btl=^openib
#
# Scheduler settings (srun --mpi type, partition, procs, walltimes) do NOT go
# here: set slurm_mpi_type / slurm_partition / <method>_partition /
# <method>_procs / <method>_walltime in config.json.
